{"name":"Sacred Ground","hex":"#b2865d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sacred","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterized by solemn religious ceremony or religious use, especially, in a positive sense; consecrated, made holy.","Religious; relating to religion, or to the services of religion; not secular"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of sacre"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacred"},{"term":"ground","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The surface of the Earth, as opposed to the sky or water or underground.","Terrain."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To connect (an electrical conductor or device) to a ground.","To electrocute."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ground"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sacred Ground (Star Trek: Voyager)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sacred Ground\" is the 49th episode of Star Trek: Voyager, the seventh episode of the third season. In this episode a crew member of the star ship Voyager is injured by an energy field in an alien temple."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacred_Ground_(Star_Trek%3A_Voyager)"},{"title":"Sacred Ground (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sacred Ground\" is a country music song, co-written and originally recorded by American country music singer Kix Brooks, prior to his joining Ronnie Dunn in the duo Brooks & Dunn. Brooks' version was issued in 1989 as a single, and was included on his 1989 self-titled debut album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/21/With_story_of_my_life.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacred_Ground_(song)"},{"title":"Sacred space","blocks":[{"text":"A sacred place or holy site is a location which is regarded to be sacred or hallowed. The sacredness of a natural feature may accrue through tradition or be granted through a blessing. One or more religions may consider sacred locations to be of special significance. Often, such locations either are or become the home of sanctuaries, shrines, places of worship, or locations conducive to meditation. Regardless of construction or use, these areas may have a variety of ritual or taboo associations – including limitations on visitors or on allowed actions within the space. Such places may become the focus of pilgrimage, drawing pilgrims from great distances, or simply locations of significance for the local populace. It is asserted by scholars of religion that \"the sacred space is the place where the transcendent becomes immanent, and where the devotee can access God.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Prayer_request_on_Stone_of_Anointing.jpg/330px-Prayer_request_on_Stone_of_Anointing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacred_space"},{"title":"Sacredness","blocks":[{"text":"Sacred describes something that is dedicated or set apart for the service or worship of a deity; is considered worthy of spiritual respect or devotion; or inspires awe or reverence among believers. The property is often ascribed to objects, or places."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacredness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Robert_Duncan_McNeill_%285777887709%29.jpg/500px-Robert_Duncan_McNeill_%285777887709%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Robert_Duncan_McNeill_%285777887709%29.jpg/1280px-Robert_Duncan_McNeill_%285777887709%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Robert_Duncan_McNeill_%285777887709%29.jpg/500px-Robert_Duncan_McNeill_%285777887709%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Star Trek: Voyager actor Robert Duncan McNeill directed his first episode.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARobert_Duncan_McNeill_(5777887709).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/27/McBride_and_the_Ride_-_Sacred_Ground_single.png/330px-McBride_and_the_Ride_-_Sacred_Ground_single.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/27/McBride_and_the_Ride_-_Sacred_Ground_single.png/330px-McBride_and_the_Ride_-_Sacred_Ground_single.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMcBride_and_the_Ride_-_Sacred_Ground_single.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/High_Priest_Offering_Sacrifice_of_a_Goat.jpg/500px-High_Priest_Offering_Sacrifice_of_a_Goat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/High_Priest_Offering_Sacrifice_of_a_Goat.jpg/500px-High_Priest_Offering_Sacrifice_of_a_Goat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The High Priest offers the sacrifice of a goat performing korban","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHigh_Priest_Offering_Sacrifice_of_a_Goat.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Westernwall2.jpg/500px-Westernwall2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Westernwall2.jpg/1280px-Westernwall2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Westernwall2.jpg/500px-Westernwall2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Western Wall, one of the last relics of the Temple in Jerusalem","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3